# 14. One subtle issue we should handle carefully

Your current MiniGPT is **character-level**.

That means it doesn't naturally have a single token corresponding to:

```text
cow
```

Instead:

```text
c → o → w
```

So when we add the semantic head, we need to decide:

> **Which Transformer hidden state represents "cow"?**

We could use the hidden state corresponding to the final character of the animal name.

For:

```text
The cow
```

we could take the hidden representation associated with:

```text
w
```

and feed it into:

```text
semantic head
```

So:

```text
"The cow"
       │
       ▼
character embeddings
       │
       ▼
Transformer
       │
       ├──────────────► language head
       │
       │
       └──────────────► semantic head
                              │
                              ▼
                        animal → verb
```

That is probably the **cleanest next experiment with your existing code**.

