# 15. And then we can make the experiment progressively more sophisticated

I would not jump immediately into pGCL or formal verification.

I'd go through these stages:

### Stage 1 — what you have now

```text
MiniGPT
    +
separate semantic classifier
    +
external guardrail
```

You've essentially completed this.

### Stage 2 — multi-task learning

```text
MiniGPT
    ├── language loss
    └── semantic loss
             ↓
         total loss
```

This demonstrates **semantic constraints influencing neural-network training**.

### Stage 3 — probabilities

Examine:

```text
P(moo | cow)
P(bark | cow)
P(meow | cow)
```

and watch how those probabilities evolve during training.

### Stage 4 — adversarial/wrong examples

Introduce:

```text
cow → bark
cow → meow
dog → moo
```

and deliberately train against them.

### Stage 5 — semantic verification

Build a verifier that asks:

```text
Does the model satisfy:

P(bark | cow) < ε ?
```

### Stage 6 — probabilistic formalization

Represent the relevant behavior as a probabilistic system.

Then we can ask:

```text
P(violation) ≤ ε
```

### Stage 7 — Isabelle/HOL / pGCL

Formalize the abstraction and attempt to prove the property.

